        "y0": 0.5881785082094597,
        "x1": 0.7805876887701695,
        "y1": 0.6007575988769531
      },
      "text": "input dimension d, by additionally exploiting geometric non-commutative properties",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2186252868253421,
        "y0": 0.6031786299715138,
        "x1": 0.7801942015005872,
        "y1": 0.6157577206390072
      },
      "text": "of some chosen m basis vector fields, owing to diffeormophism controllability results",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.21862543642131332,
        "y0": 0.618330145123029,
        "x1": 0.2860761405595767,
        "y1": 0.6309092357905224
      },
      "text": "due to [1].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2429393194859324,
        "y0": 0.6334816602745441,
        "x1": 0.7803898730309181,
        "y1": 0.6460607509420375
      },
      "text": "Our goal in this paper is to derive quantitative rates of approximation of (1). Exist-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
