        "y0": 0.6786329565626202,
        "x1": 0.7803915933845869,
        "y1": 0.6912120472301136
      },
      "text": "ested in quantitative rates for approximation of flow maps in the uniform norm. The",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.21862603480519813,
        "y0": 0.6937844717141354,
        "x1": 0.7807823629940257,
        "y1": 0.7063635623816288
      },
      "text": "problem we address is how many switches are needed in A(t),W (t),b(t), to approx-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.21862683265037786,
        "y0": 0.7089359868656505,
        "x1": 0.36151990703507964,
        "y1": 0.7215150775331439
      },
      "text": "imate the flow of (3).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3707838370129953,
        "y0": 0.7089359868656505,
        "x1": 0.6562259649139603,
        "y1": 0.7215150775331439
      },
      "text": "In this way, our result complements [9, 2].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
